# CQRS + MediatR Patterns

## Folder layout (one folder per endpoint)

Place each command/query with its handler + validator under `Commands/` or `Queries/`, grouped by API route group and endpoint:

```text
Application/
  Commands/
    Auth/
      Login/              LoginCommand.cs, LoginCommandHandler.cs, LoginCommandValidator.cs
      ForgotPassword/
      AcceptInvitation/
    Users/
      InviteUser/
    Tenants/
      CreateTenant/
  Queries/
    Auth/
      GetCurrentUser/     GetCurrentUserQuery.cs, GetCurrentUserQueryHandler.cs
    Audit/
      ListAuditLogs/
    Platform/
      Ping/
```

Namespace matches the path, e.g. `SchoolSaaS.Application.Commands.Auth.Login` or `SchoolSaaS.Application.Queries.Auth.GetCurrentUser`.

Shared abstractions stay in `Application/Abstractions/`. Cross-cutting behaviors stay in `Application/Behaviors/`.

## Command Template

```csharp
// Application/Commands/Students/CreateStudent/CreateStudentCommand.cs
namespace SchoolSaaS.Application.Commands.Students.CreateStudent;

public sealed record CreateStudentCommand(string FirstName, string LastName, Guid ClassId)
    : ICommand<Guid>;

// CreateStudentCommandHandler.cs — same folder
public sealed class CreateStudentCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<CreateStudentCommand, Result<Guid>> { ... }

// CreateStudentCommandValidator.cs — same folder
public sealed class CreateStudentCommandValidator : AbstractValidator<CreateStudentCommand> { }
```

## Query Rules

- Queries are **read-only** — no `SaveChanges`, no domain events.
- Apply scope filtering via `IScopeResolver` in handler.
- Return DTOs, never domain entities, from query handlers.

## MediatR Pipeline Behaviors (already registered — do not bypass)

Order: `LoggingBehavior` → `ValidationBehavior` → `AuthorizationBehavior` → `TenantBehavior` → `AuditBehavior` → Handler

## IRequest vs INotification

- `IRequest<Result<T>>` — commands and queries (single handler)
- `INotification` — domain events with multiple handlers
